{
  "rationale": "The plant is split into sensing and motion capability so the supervisor can react to uncontrollable obstacle observations before issuing one-shot motion pulses. The specifications encode a progress-biased exploration policy: use forward motion in clear conditions, use directed short turns for side obstacles, use a brief backward escape only for front obstacles, and return to forward exploration immediately when path_clear is observed. Action states self-loop on path_clear so the intended pulse is not preempted in the same step, while obstacle events can still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability in G",
    "Use small deterministic specifications to bind sensed conditions to exactly one allowed controllable action per decision state",
    "Bias clear-space behavior to move_forward rather than rotate or back up",
    "Use rotate_clockwise for left-side blockage and rotate_counterclockwise for right-side blockage consistently",
    "Reserve move_backward for dedicated front-obstacle recovery only, then transition to a turn recovery state",
    "Return to clear exploration as soon as path_clear occurs after recovery"
  ],
